            answer: "A",
            explanation: "`hasNextLine()` returns `true` while there is another line to read in the file, and `false` once the Scanner has reached end-of-file. This is how the standard while-loop pattern `while (sc.hasNextLine()) { ... }` knows when to stop reading. Options A, B, and C confuse the return type or invent values not in the Scanner API. The method is the natural companion to `nextLine()` for line-by-line reading.",
